Browser automation

Install:
  Install the missing skill and CLI; prepare Node.js, pnpm and Git as needed and set up Chromium with the CLI.

Upgrade:
  Back up and replace the installed skill; update the installed CLI and refresh Chromium, restoring previous skill files if browser setup fails.

Status:
  Report skill locations based on SKILL.md presence and the CLI command location and version; Chromium readiness is not checked.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Source: https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser
  Destination: ~/.agents/skills/agent-browser
  Existing copies at ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/agent-browser are consolidated into links to the destination when skill files are replaced.
  Browser files and Linux dependencies are set up when installing or upgrading the CLI; installation preserves an existing CLI and browser setup.
  Browser maintenance commands: agent-browser --help
